`); }, projectId: config.projectId, provider: providerFor(process.env["MOE_AGENT_COMMAND"] ?? "claude")?.leaf ?? "claude", store: verifierStore, }),` - the command resolves exactly as the spawner resolves it (agent-spawner.ts:49 `options.command ?? process.env["MOE_AGENT_COMMAND"] ?? "claude"`); an unknown command reads as "claude" (child 3's scripted seat double prints the claude line under a non-claude command) - say so in a one-line comment. Keep the block's closing at 6-space indent (`      }),`) so agent-wrapper-main.test.ts's `wrapperCall` slice (ends at the first `
    });`) still spans the whole call. (2) The idle line at agent-wrapper-main.ts:386: `const idle = report.paused === undefined ? <today's line unchanged> : `[wrapper] provider paused: ${report.paused.provider} until ${report.paused.resetAt} (active ${String(report.active)})
`;` - the existing once-per-distinct-state `lastIdle` mechanism prints it once per pause, not once per poll. (3) apps/daemon/src/orchestrator/agent-wrapper-main.test.ts, describe "wrapper binary staffing wiring": add `it("passes a providerPause built from the real store in the production createAgentWrapper call")` asserting `wrapperCall(SOURCE)` toContain `providerPause: createProviderPauseGate({` and, within the providerPause block, `store: verifierStore` and `providerFor(process.env["MOE_AGENT_COMMAND"]`, plus `.not.toContain("providerPause: undefined")`; a positive control that strips `providerPause: createProviderPauseGate({` and expects the assertion to throw; and `expect(SOURCE).toContain("[wrapper] provider paused:")` for the idle line. Gate from apps/daemon: `pnpm exec vitest run --root . --config package.json src/orchestrator/agent-wrapper-main.test.ts` (count line quoted) + `pnpm --filter @moe/daemon typecheck`.
